{"title":"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three players, Ava, Beau, and Cato, are playing a tournament. Each person plays exactly two games, one game against each of the other players. If a game ends in a tie, both players are awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point. Otherwise, the winning player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> points and the losing player is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points.\n</p><p>For example, if the tournament results are as shown below and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/9/129a394e53ae5d9485467a5da722ed2d61c63077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W = 2$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, then points are awarded as follows:\n</p><p>(add a table to the Problem 2 page)\n</p><p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is equal to the sum of the points that have been awarded to the three players when the tournament has finished. In the example above, Ava is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point, Beau is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, and Cato is awarded <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae948412b3206828fd197dbd41fd8a41bf7c4de5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> in the example.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Parts\">Parts</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Parts\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a\">2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b\">2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2c\">2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2c</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2d\" title=\"2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2d\">2025 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2d</a></li></ul>\n\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017032017\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time u